{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) < ndim(v_2) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) + i)) else if ndim(v_2) < ndim(v_1) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) + i))
>>
Rule 74 (Shape of at least one tensor has to be less than 6)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) < 6 ∨ ndim(v_2) < 6
>>
Rule 75 (If two tensors are boolean and share a same shape[i], the value should be same.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = "bool") ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = "bool") then if ndim(v_1) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1,i) = shape(v_2,i))
>>
Rule 76 (If one tensor's shape has 0, then the other tensor's shape has to be either [] or all of its shape[i] equal to 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1] : shape(v_1,i) = 0) then (ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1)) else if (ndim(v_2) > 0) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2)-1] : shape(v_2,i) = 0) then (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 78 (At least one dimension size of two tensors should be more than zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)) ∨ (ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0)
>>
Rule 79 (If v1 is of float16, float32, float64 type, the v2 has to of numerical type or boolean)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = "float16") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "float32") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "float64") then (dtype_(v_2) = "int" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "float" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "complex64" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "complex128" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "bool")
>>
Rule 80 (If v2 is of float16, float32, float64 type, the v1 has to of numerical type or boolean)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_2) = "float16") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "float32") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "float64") then (dtype_(v_1) = "int" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "float" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "complex64" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "complex128" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "bool")
>>
Rule 81 (If both dimensions are greater than 0, and one dimension is equal to 1, then the shape[i] of one tensor either equal to another tensor or to 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0) ∧ (ndim(v_2) > 0) then ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) < ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) else ndim(v_2) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 82 (v_1's dtype must be numeric, can be int, float or complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = "int") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "float16") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "float32") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "float64") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "complex64") ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = "complex128")
>>
Rule 83 (v_2's dtype must be numeric, can be int, float or complex)
{v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_2) = "int") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "float16") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "float32") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "float64") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "complex64") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "complex128")
>>
Rule 85 (The data type of either input tensor can be boolean, and if so, the output tensor must be boolean too)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = "bool") ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = "bool")
>>
Rule 86 (if one of the tensors is boolean, then the other one's type has to be int or float)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = "bool" then (dtype_(v_2) = "int" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "float16" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "float32" ∨ dtype_(v_2) = "float64") else if dtype_(v_2) = "bool" then (dtype_(v_1) = "int" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "float16" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "float32" ∨ dtype_(v_1) = "float64")
>>
Rule 87 (If both tensors share rank and any dimension, the data type should be same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) then dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 88 (if the first tensor's shape is [a, b], and second tensor's shape is [c,d], it should meet the following requirement: either a and c are equal, or c equal 1, or d equals 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1
>>
Rule 89 (if the first tensor's shape is [a], the second one should be broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then (ndim(v_2) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 2)
>>
Rule 90 (if the second tensor's shape is [a], the first one should be broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = 1 then (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2)
